# Standalone guided walk through bob/capture — a SearchTextRequest whose
# type was inferred, whose score is not perfect, and whose first text_query
# is shadowed by a second.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture
#
# Positional paths:
#   /    SearchTextRequest root (inferred, score −8)
#   /1   text_query: "<binary blob>"  — the shadowed first instance
#   /2   text_query: "coffee in Grenoble"  #@ repeated_singular
#   /3   language_code: "en-US"
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: What is bob/capture?

steps:
  - text: |
      protolens opened without a type name and found one anyway:

        👉 SearchTextRequest.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      Hover over the "SearchTextRequest" type name.

      A score breakdown tooltip appears.
      Note the penalty for "non-canonical encoding".

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      Here is the issue.  text_query appears twice.

      The schema declares it singular — press `v` to verify.
      But the wire carries two instances of the field...
      Last one wins: protoc shows you "coffee in Grenoble" and silently drops the 1st instance.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    select_line: true
    search: text_query

  - text: |
      protolens annotates the second text_query as repeated_singular.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    select_line: true
    search: repeated_singular

  - text: |
      The first text_query gets shadowed. protolens annotates it as such.

      Press `$` to see the `#@ shadowed_scalar` annotation at the right edge of the line.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      While we are here, play with the navigation arrows.
      And click on the node fold-togglers.
      These are the basic commands to navigate a protobuf in protolens.

      You can also press a number on a node to set the folding level.

      👋 Press space to step when you are done.

    node: /1

  - text: |
      Press Enter to quit.

    node: /1
    command: quit
